{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:6780551 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:6780551 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"6780551","source":"MED","pmid":"6780551","doi":"10.1016/s0021-9258(19)69841-8","title":"Evolutionarily homologous alpha 2 beta 2 oligomeric structures in beta-ketoadipate succinyl-CoA transferases from Acinetobacter calcoaceticus and Pseudomonas putida.","authorString":"Yeh WK, Ornston LN.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Yeh WK","lastName":"Yeh","firstName":"W K","initials":"WK"},{"fullName":"Ornston LN","lastName":"Ornston","firstName":"L N","initials":"LN"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"4","volume":"256","journalIssueId":374865,"dateOfPublication":"1981 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":1981,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Biol Chem","title":"The Journal of biological chemistry","essn":"1083-351X","issn":"0021-9258","isoabbreviation":"J Biol Chem","nlmid":"2985121R"},"printPublicationDate":"1981-02-01"},"pubYear":"1981","pageInfo":"1565-1569","abstractText":"Homogeneous beta-ketoadipate succinyl-CoA transferase (EC 2.8.3.6) preparations were obtained from extracts of Acinetobacter calcoaceticus and Pseudomonas putida. Gel filtration indicated that the respective transferases have similar molecular weights of 108,000 and 109,000; each transferase appears to have an alpha 2 beta 2 oligomeric structure formed by association of nonidentical subunits with a molecular weight of about 25,000. The subunits were separated by sodium dodecyl sulfate-gel electrophoresis, and differences in their primary structures were revealed by determination of the NH2-terminal amino acid sequences of the oligomers. The transferases cross-react immunologically and possess similar amino acid compositions. These are remarkably similar to the amino acid compositions of gamma-carboxymuconolactone decarboxylases (EC 4.1.1.44) and beta-ketoadipate enol-lactone hydrolases (EC 3.1.1.24), enzymes that mediate consecutive reactions preceding the transferase step in the beta-ketoadipate pathway.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Comparative Study","Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S.","Research Support, U.S. Gov't, Non-P.H.S.","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"GM 25487","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Acinetobacter","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pseudomonas","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Macromolecular Substances"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Coenzyme A-Transferases"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Sulfurtransferases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IP","qualifierName":"isolation & purification"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Immune Sera"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Immunoassay"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Immunodiffusion"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Species Specificity"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Amino Acid Sequence"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Molecular Weight"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Biological Evolution"}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"3-oxoadipate CoA-transferase","registryNumber":"EC 2.8.3.6"},{"name":"Immune Sera","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Macromolecular Substances","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Sulfurtransferases","registr